WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Speaker 1: Hey, one quick note. Madison&nbsp;
Cawthorn, thankfully as one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.200
radical members of Congress to be elected in&nbsp;
2020, was defeated in a Republican primary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.360
Good. He'll be leaving on January, whatever&nbsp;
the date is, 2023, when the new Congress is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.040
inaugurated. Except it appears that he has&nbsp;
already left. There's a very interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:26.640
report from The Citizen Times. Madison Cawthorn&nbsp;
vacates office before end of term constituents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.260
calls go unanswered. He has stopped working.&nbsp;
Madison Cawthorn is no longer working. He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.720
still an elected official. He's still a member of&nbsp;
Congress. He isn't working anymore. And this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.440
just really instructive about what happens when&nbsp;
you vote for these people. None of these people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.740
want to work. This is the exact same story as&nbsp;
what we saw with Donald Trump during the campaign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:54.300
